fect of video game design theory in the creation of game-based systems for upper limb stroke rehabilitation. JMIR Serious Games, 7(2), e12131."}]," ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6453078/","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":["Read source ",["$","$Lf",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$1d:props:children:0:props:children:0:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-external-link","size":13}]]}]]}],["$","li","gaming-fit-2025",{"id":"reference-gaming-fit-2025","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Ballou, N., Vuorre, M., Hakman, T., Magnusson, K., & Przybylski, A. K. (2025). Perceived value of video games, but not hours played, predicts mental well-being in casual adult Nintendo players. Royal Society Open Science, 12(3)."}]," ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1098/rsos.241174","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":["Read source ",["$","$Lf",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$1d:props:children:0:props:children:0:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-external-link","size":13}]]}]]}]]}]]}]
